 }
 
+/* ── the strip stopped fitting, and took the whole page with it ───────────
+ *
+ * MEASURED, NOT REASONED. `pnpm audit:rendered` at 320px: the document scrolls
+ * sideways on every page of the site, and .ub-phone — the last item in this row
+ * — sits at 329→430px inside a 320px viewport. Not a rounding error: the row is
+ * roughly 130px of hours + 79 "Service areas" + 49 "Reviews" + 101 phone + gaps
+ * + 40 of padding, every item white-space:nowrap, in 320 available.
+ *
+ * A horizontal scrollbar on a phone is not a cosmetic defect. Every section of
+ * every page is then ~110px wider than the screen, text runs off the right edge
+ * mid-sentence, and the visitor drags the page back and forth to read a line.
+ * It is the single worst thing a layout can do on mobile and it was on the
+ * home page.
+ *
+ * The block above already states the right principle — "keeps the two facts
+ * that convert and drops the rest" — and then drops three of six items, which
+ * is enough at 720px and not at 320. The two facts are the hours and the phone
+ * number. Service areas and Reviews are in the footer and in the mega-menu on
+ * every page, exactly as the note above says.
+ *
+ * The ellipsis is the belt to that braces: if HOURS_LINE_SHORT is ever
+ * lengthened, the hours truncate and the phone number stays put, rather than
+ * the whole document growing a scrollbar again. min-width:0 is what lets a flex
+ * item shrink below its content — without it text-overflow never fires. */
+@media (max-width: 430px) {
+  .ub-link { display: none; }
+  .ub-hours { min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
+  .ub-phone { flex: 0 0 auto; }
+}
+
 /* ── the mega-menu ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
